UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4, Week 20, Lesson 2: Creating a multimodal persuasive presentation', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Creating a multimodal persuasive presentation means aligning spoken words, on-screen text and images so they support one honest message.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same strategy to an unfamiliar topic or audience, then compare the effect of two different choices.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nPlan three modes for a \"walk to school Wednesday\" pitch.\n\nFEEDBACK\nImage of safe route; short bullets; spoken reasons — keep claims honest.\n\nCHECK\nDecorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nBuild a 3-slide multimodal pitch with aligned speech notes. Label each mode’s job and one honesty check you applied.\n\nWrite a short reflection describing one specific revision you made and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"English","learning_intention":"Creating a multimodal persuasive presentation means aligning spoken words, on-screen text and images so they support one honest message.","lesson_number":2,"lesson_role":"Writing","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN2-CWT-03"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Build a 3-slide multimodal pitch with aligned speech notes. Label each mode’s job and one honesty check you applied. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Image of safe route; short bullets; spoken reasons — keep claims honest. Reasoning: I used multimodal by attending to presentation rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Decorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience. Correction: Image of safe route; short bullets; spoken reasons — keep claims honest. Why: the correction restores accurate use of multimodal.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Decorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating multimodal on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with multimodal, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Image of safe route; short bullets; spoken reasons — keep claims honest. This matches the lesson skill for multimodal.","options":["Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work.","Image of safe route; short bullets; spoken reasons — keep claims honest.","Decorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event."],"question":"Plan three modes for a \"walk to school Wednesday\" pitch. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Decorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson idea.","options":["Image of safe route; short bullets; spoken reasons — keep claims honest.","Careful use of presentation with clear evidence.","Decorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience.","Creating a multimodal persuasive presentation means aligning spoken words, on-screen text and images so they support one honest message."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when practising multimodal?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and named presentation, not by copying the model.","options":["Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Choose randomly because any option could be right.","Treat a missing detail as a stated fact.","Apply the idea with new evidence and name the presentation used."],"question":"A learner is practising multimodal. Which approach best shows understanding?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries multimodal.","options":["Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event.","Say the writing is good without naming any words.","Decorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience.","Point to exact words in the sentence that show multimodal and say what they do."],"question":"Read: \"When the ferry horn blasted, Omar gripped the railing and laughed.\" Which choice best uses multimodal from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill; the others miss the evidence.","options":["Image of safe route; short bullets; spoken reasons — keep claims honest.","Decorative images that contradict the claim confuse the audience.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event.","Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work."],"question":"Which statement correctly applies the lesson idea about multimodal?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Start from a specific textual clue, then explain its effect.","options":["Guess from the title alone w